COIS- Declarations. Human Ethics and Consent to Participate: This retrospective study 
      was approved by the Scientific and Ethics Committee of the AP-HP Clinical Data 
      Warehouse (IRB00011591, CSE n degrees 24-37) and complied with the French MR-004 
      reference methodology governing the reuse of healthcare data for research. 
      Patients were individually informed of the potential reuse of their clinical data 
      and could object; hence, formal written consent was not required. Only patients 
      who had consulted or been hospitalized at least once between August 1st, 2017 and 
      January 29th, 2025 and had received this information were included. Declaration 
      of the Use of Generative AI and AI-Assisted Technologies: The authors used 
      OpenAI''s ChatGPT (GPT-5, accessed in December 2025) solely to generate fictional 
      illustrative clinical texts, to demonstrate the algorithm''s functionality 
      without disclosing real patient data. Representative prompts included requests to 
      generate realistic but entirely fictional French-language medical reports 
      mentioning sickle cell disease genotypes. No real patient data were used as 
      input. The generated texts were reviewed and edited by the authors, who take full 
      responsibility for the final content. No generative AI tool was used for the 
      analysis, the design of the algorithm, or the scientific writing of the 
      manuscript. Competing Interests: The authors declare no competing interests.
