COIS- Declarations. Ethics approval and consent to participate: Approval for the study 
      was obtained from the Joint CUHAS-Bugando/BMC Research Committee and the Medical 
      Officer in charge of Sengerema DDH. Participants were informed about the study's 
      purpose, risks, and benefits, and consent was required for participation. 
      Illiterate participants provided a thumbprint as consent. Confidentiality was 
      assured, and participants could withdraw at any time without affecting their 
      healthcare. For those under 18 years, consent was obtained from parents or 
      guardians. Participants answered questions using structured questionnaires in 
      English and Swahili. Symptomatic and asymptomatic women with peripheral malaria 
      and anemia received treatment following national guidelines. Consent for 
      publication: Not applicable. Competing interests: The authors declare no 
      competing interests.
