TI  - Sharp bounds on the relative treatment effect for ordinal outcomes.
PG  - 664-669
LID - 10.1111/biom.13148 [doi]
AB  - For ordinal outcomes, the average treatment effect is often ill-defined and hard 
      to interpret. Echoing Agresti and Kateri, we argue that the relative treatment 
      effect can be a useful measure, especially for ordinal outcomes, which is defined 
      as gamma = prYi(1) > Yi(0) - prYi(1) < Yi(0) , with Yi(1) and Yi(0) being the 
      potential outcomes of unit i under treatment and control, respectively. Given the 
      marginal distributions of the potential outcomes, we derive the sharp bounds on 
      gamma,  which are identifiable parameters based on the observed data. Agresti and 
      Kateri focused on modeling strategies under the assumption of independent 
      potential outcomes, but we allow for arbitrary dependence.
