TI  - Probability of premature death for chronic non-communicable diseases, Brazil and 
      Regions, projections to 2025.
PG  - e190030
LID - S1415-790X2019000100428 [pii]
LID - 10.1590/1980-549720190030 [doi]
AB  - OBJECTIVE: Objective: To analyze the mortality trends for Chronic Noncommunicable 
      Diseases (NCDs) in the period 2000-2013 and its probability of death until 2025. 
      METHOD: time series analysis of mortality from cardiovascular diseases, cancer, 
      diabetes and chronic respiratory disease, with correction for ill-defined causes 
      and underreporting of deaths and calculation of probability of death. RESULTS: 
      There was an average decline of 2.5% per year in all four major NCDs in Brazil. 
      There was a decline in all regions and federal units. The reduced likelihood of 
      death by 30% in 2000 to 26.1% in 2013 and expected decline to 20.5% in 2025. 
      CONCLUSION: From the trend of reduction is expected to reach Brazil reducing 
      overall goal 25% by 2025.
