TI  - Use of Verbal Autopsy to Determine Underlying Cause of Death during Treatment of 
      Multidrug-Resistant Tuberculosis, India.
PG  - 478-484
LID - 10.3201/eid2403.171718 [doi]
AB  - Of patients with multidrug-resistant tuberculosis (MDR TB), <50% complete 
      treatment. Most treatment failures for patients with MDR TB are due to death 
      during TB treatment. We sought to determine the proportion of deaths during MDR 
      TB treatment attributable to TB itself. We used a structured verbal autopsy tool 
      to interview family members of patients who died during MDR TB treatment in India 
      during January-December 2016. A committee triangulated information from verbal 
      autopsy, death certificate, or other medical records available with the family 
      members to ascertain the underlying cause of death. For 66% of patient deaths 
      (47/71), TB was the underlying cause of death. We assigned TB as the underlying 
      cause of death for an additional 6 patients who died of suicide and 2 of 
      pulmonary embolism. Deaths during TB treatment signify program failure; 
      accurately determining the cause of death is the first step to designing 
      appropriate, timely interventions to prevent premature deaths.
