TI  - Utility and Limitations of Large Population-Based Data for Skin Cancer Outcomes.
PG  - 2128-2130
LID - S0022-202X(16)32249-7 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.jid.2016.07.031 [doi]
AB  - Large population-based studies are useful for determining cancer outcomes, but 
      interpreting their findings requires understanding their limitations. Youlden 
      et al. highlight the utility of using a large dataset for studying melanoma 
      survival, whereas Gimotty et al. point out the limitations of such datasets in 
      miscoding thickness, a key prognostic variable. Awareness of limitations of 
      population-based registry data can help to inform their interpretations and 
      clinical implications.
