TI  - The Chronic Kidney Disease Epidemiology Collaboration (CKD-EPI) equation 
      incorporating both cystatin C and creatinine best predicts individual risk: a 
      cohort study in 444 patients with chronic kidney disease.
PG  - 348-55
LID - 10.1093/ndt/gft422 [doi]
AB  - BACKGROUND: The recently introduced CKD-EPIcreat-cys equation surpassed 
      creatinine-based equations for GFR estimation in a large cross-sectional 
      analysis. However, its performance to predict individual risk of CKD progression 
      and death in patients with various underlying CKD etiologies is unknown. METHODS: 
      We recruited 444 patients with CKD GFR categories 2-4 (eGFR 15-89 mL/min/1.73 
      m2); baseline eGFR was estimated by the established MDRD and CKD-EPIcreat 
      equations and by the novel CKD-EPIcreat-cys equation. RESULTS: Patients were 
      followed for 2.7+/-1.2 years for the occurrence of the combined predefined endpoint 
      event: death, need for renal replacement therapy or halving of eGFR. The endpoint 
      occurred in 62 patients. Reclassification from MDRD determined categories to 
      CKD-EPIcreat-cys categories yielded net reclassification improvements for those 
      with the endpoint event (NRIevents) of 27.4% (95% CI: 16.7-40.0%) and for those 
      without the event (NRInon-events) of -3.1% (-8.2 to 1.6%). Similarly, 
      reclassification from CKD-EPIcreat categories to CKD-EPIcreat-cys categories 
      yielded an NRIevents of 22.6% (10.2-34.3%) and NRInon-events of -11.3% (-15.9 to 
      -6.5%). Addition of albuminuria to each eGFR equation increased the calculated 
      risk of the outcome for a net 26-32% of those who subsequently reached the 
      endpoint, and reduced the calculated risk in a net 21-23% in non-event patients, 
      but only minimally. CONCLUSIONS: The CKD-EPIcreat-cys equation assigned patients 
      who went on to have the event to more appropriate CKD risk categories than MDRD 
      and CKD-EPIcreat, but patients without the event to less appropriate categories 
      than CKD-EPIcreat. Addition of albuminuria marginally improved risk 
      classification for those who had the event.
