TI  - RETRACTED: Syncope in adults with pulmonary arterial hypertension.
PG  - 863-7
LID - 10.1016/j.jacc.2011.04.026 [doi]
AB  - This article has been retracted: please see Elsevier Policy on Article Withdrawal 
      (http://www.elsevier.com/locate/withdrawalpolicy). This article has been 
      retracted at the request of the authors, because of a data entry error which is 
      fundamental to the study findings. As background, this was a clinical study where 
      a specific variable was tested in a large database. The process involved merging 
      a variable (presence or absence of syncope) from one electronic source with an 
      alternate electronic database of patients with pulmonary arterial hypertension 
      and assessing associations and outcomes. In proceeding to design a follow-up 
      study to this work Dr. Le, went back to the original source file to abstract new 
      data. In doing this she identified a 'cut-and paste' error in which the column of 
      syncope data was transferred incorrectly where syncope/no syncope variables were 
      assigned to wrong subjects. This led to a critical error that then got carried 
      forward and a fundamental misclassification of syncope in the final study group. 
      This error fundamentally affects the results which now do not fully support the 
      conclusions.
