TI  - Deaths caused by HIV disease under-reported in South Africa.
PG  - 1600-2
LID - 10.1097/QAD.0b013e32832d4719 [doi]
AB  - Modelling of trends in age-specific death rates in South Africa suggests that 
      deaths attributable to HIV are often misclassified on death notification forms. 
      We compared the underlying cause of death from death notification forms with that 
      based on scrutiny of medical records for 683 deaths in Cape Town. Of 129 deaths 
      caused by HIV according to medical records, only 35 (27.1%) were ascribed to HIV 
      on the death notification form using strict coding and 83 (64.3%) using 
      interpretive coding.
