TI  - Endovascular management of acute enteric bleeding from pancreas transplant.
PG  - 313-6
AB  - Arterioenteric fistula is a rare but serious complication of enteric drained 
      pancreas transplant, which may lead to massive gastrointestinal bleeding. We 
      present 3 patients with failed enteric drained pancreas transplants and massive 
      gastrointestinal bleeding secondary to arterioenteric fistula. One patient was 
      treated by embolization and the 2 others by stent graft placement. Bleeding was 
      successfully controlled in all cases, at follow up of 5 days, 8 months, and 12 
      months, respectively. One patient died 24 days after embolization, of unknown 
      causes.
