TI  - An in-depth look at Krukenberg tumor: an overview.
PG  - 1725-30
AB  - Krukenberg tumor is an uncommon metastatic tumor of the ovary. This article 
      provides an overview of the major pathologic manifestations of Krukenberg tumor, 
      patient characteristics, clinical and laboratory features of the disease, 
      prognostic factors, and current knowledge about its pathogenesis. Pathologists 
      have to be familiar with the diagnostic histopathologic features of the tumor and 
      its principal differential diagnoses. Awareness of the diagnostic manifestations 
      of the tumor leads to the correct diagnosis and prevents tumor misclassification, 
      thus avoiding improper clinical management. The article also addresses the 
      potential clinical utility of serum CA 125 in patients with Krukenberg tumors. 
      Prognosis of Krukenberg tumor is still very poor but our review of the literature 
      reveals several factors that appear to have an impact on survival. There is no 
      established treatment for Krukenberg tumors. A national registry and prospective 
      studies are needed to set a therapeutic approach for Krukenberg tumors in the 
      hope of improving the survival rate.
