TI  - Insulinoma--a case report.
PG  - 540-1
AB  - Insulinoma is a rare pancreatic endocrine tumour characterised by 
      hyperinsulinemic hypoglycemia. It is important to surgically remove this tumour 
      as it can cause potentially lethal hypoglycemia. We report a case of insulinoma 
      presenting with unconsciousness following repeated episodes of inability to arise 
      from sleep and convulsions. Biochemical investigation revealed hypoglycemia and 
      hyperinsulinemia. The diagnosis of Insulinoma is often delayed due to 
      misattribution of symptoms to psychiatric or neurological disorders. In this 
      case, same delay lead to fatal outcome for this patient.
