TI  - Urethral transitional cell carcinoma in a cat.
PG  - 504-6
AB  - A 15-year-old, male neutered cat was referred for investigation of dysuria. A 
      retrograde urethrography was performed which showed two space-occupying masses 
      within the lumen of the mid-to-proximal urethra. Exploratory coeliotomy revealed 
      two urethral masses. Segmental urethrectomy was performed to resect the mass, and 
      the lower urinary tract was reconstructed by vesico-urethral anastomosis. 
      Histopathology showed the mass to be a transitional cell carcinoma with 
      incomplete surgical margins. Tumour regrowth was suspected when dysuria was found 
      approximately 318 days after surgery. Clinical signs were palliated by radiation 
      using weekly fractions of 6 Gy for three weeks. The cat died of unknown causes 
      386 days postoperatively.
