TI  - Analysis of undetectable HIV RNA using survival analysis: results must be 
      interpreted carefully.
PG  - 417-20
AB  - This methodological note exemplifies the drawbacks of conventional survival 
      analysis for studying the determinants of the evolution of HIV RNA after the 
      initiation of a HAART regimen in observational cohort studies. The potential for 
      loss of information might yield differential misclassification biases and 
      therefore unreliable results. Longitudinal models are better suited to analyze 
      the repeated measures of a continuous outcome such as HIV RNA.
