TI  - A population at high risk for esophageal cancer in the north-east of Italy.
PG  - 355-63
AB  - Esophageal cancer is generally characterised by relatively low incidence and 
      mortality rates in Europe. However, a high-risk population for this tumour is 
      resident in the north-east of Italy. Several studies have been conducted on this 
      population of males confirming the major role of alcohol and tobacco consumption 
      alone and in combination. The inhabitants of this area of Italy constitute an 
      ideal target population for studies of molecular epidemiology aimed at 
      elucidating the natural history of the disease which is still ill-defined, and 
      the distribution of genetic alterations at a population level.
