TI  - Primary leptomeningeal astrocytoma. Case report.
PG  - 586-9
AB  - Gliomas very rarely arise from the leptomeninges. They can be both solitary and 
      diffuse, and histological examination reveals mostly astrocytic tumors. The 
      authors report a case (the 12th reported in the literature) of a solitary primary 
      glioma of the leptomeninges in a 79-year-old man who presented with repeated 
      seizures. A magnetic resonance image revealed an ill-defined enhancing lesion in 
      the cerebral meninges. Autopsy examination showed a poorly demarcated astrocytoma 
      in the sylvian fissure infiltrating the adjacent subarachnoid space. The 
      literature concerning primary leptomeningeal glioma is reviewed.
