TI  - Screening of somatization disorder: validation of the Spanish version of the 
      Othmer and DeSouza test.
PG  - 411-5
AB  - The objective of this study was to validate the Spanish version of the Othmer and 
      DeSouza Screening Test for Somatization Disorder. We have designed a validity 
      study using the Standardized Polyvalent Psychiatric Interview, an instrument 
      specifically designed to diagnose psychiatric morbidity in medical settings as 
      the 'golden rule'. The control group displayed 'functional' and 'presenting' 
      somatization. The Othmer and DeSouza Screening Test, with a threshold of three 
      symptoms, shows 88% sensitivity, 78% specificity and a misclassification rate of 
      17%. It is concluded that Othmer and DeSouza's screening test, with a threshold 
      of three symptoms, is a useful tool for the diagnosis of somatization disorder in 
      medical and primary care settings in Spain. Discrepancies with US findings are 
      discussed on a cross-cultural basis.
