TI  - Supraventricular tachycardia. Occasional nuisance or frequent threat?
PG  - 21-5
AB  - Supraventricular tachycardias (SVTs) are common and are widely regarded as a 
      nuisance. They are often repetitive and persistent, and cause more upset than is 
      currently acknowledged although only rarely do they threaten life. Surprisingly, 
      they are ill-defined. A modern approach to SVT requires an accurate diagnosis and 
      a readiness to abandon obsolete therapies in favour of effective new strategies, 
      whether pharmacological or ablative.
