TI  - Multifocal Ewing's sarcoma and hypercalcemia. A case report.
PG  - 254-8
AB  - An unusual case of Ewing's sarcoma in which the earliest sign of disease was the 
      development of hypercalcemia is described. Radiologic examinations showed 
      extensive osteolysis involving all of the trunk, and the proximal femora and 
      humeri. An ill defined destruction of the left fibula was also noted. No definite 
      primary site was found. The lungs and other visceral organs were free of 
      metastasis. To the best of the author's knowledge, no comparable case has been 
      reported in the literature.
