TI  - Autopsy cases among patients with mental disorders: an unusual case of asphyxia 
      caused by the iron roller of a garbage truck.
PG  - 896-9
AB  - A case of asphyxia of a young man suffering from "Identity Disorder" as 
      delineated by the DSM-III-R (American Psychiatric Association's Diagnostic and 
      Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders revised in 1987) is reported. The patient 
      jumped into the drum of a garbage truck and the iron roller in the drum 
      asphyxiated him by compression. In addition to the presentation of this rare 
      category of the DSM-III-R disorders as an autopsy case and an unusual means of 
      asphyxia, we briefly reviewed other autopsy cases of the patients with mental 
      disorders who died in Japan between 1988 and 1992.
