DP  - 1993 Dec
TI  - Classification of death in patients under antiarrhythmic treatment.
PG  - 2250-4
AB  - In the evaluation of antiarrhythmic treatment, total mortality and total cardiac 
      mortality are the only endpoints difficult to misclassify. End-stage cardiac 
      failure competes with "suddenness" in many instances of sudden arrhythmic death. 
      This observational study reports on 23 deaths in a group of 129 patients under 
      antiarrhythmic treatment. In the 21 cases of cardiac death, with respect to the 
      notion "sudden arrhythmic death," classification was problematic in 6 patients. 
      According to different interpretations, the number of deaths listed as "sudden" 
      could vary between one and six. A concise description of cause and circumstances 
      of death, is presented.
