TI  - Undetected drug addict fatalities.
PG  - 157-9
AB  - A urine screening in fatalities with an unnatural or unknown cause of death 
      (13-40 years of age) was carried out to evaluate the proportion of undetected 
      drug-related cases. Ten out of 160 fatalities without a hint of drug consumption 
      were classified as drug-related according to the definition of the 
      Bundeskriminalamt; 5 of them committed suicide. Moreover, we found a relevant 
      amount of AIDS deaths from the risk group of intravenous drug addicts not 
      registered as drug-related deaths.
