TI  - [Upper digestive hemorrhage in patients older than 60 years of age].
PG  - 53-6
AB  - We reviewed 286 records of patients older than 60 years with upper GI bleeding 
      from 1985 to 1990. The average age was 72.7 +/- 8.9 y. The most common etiologies 
      were: Gastric Ulcer 26%, Erosive gastritis 24%, Esophageal varices 16%, Duodenal 
      Ulcer 13%, Miscellaneous 17% and Unknown causes 3%. Global mortality rate was 38% 
      and the most frequent cause was variceal bleeding in 36%.
