TI  - Poisson regression with misclassified counts: application to cervical cancer.
PG  - 81-93
AB  - "Errors in disease classification can give misleading inferences for covariate 
      effects when the probability of error is itself related to the covariates. More 
      accurate inferences are possible using supplemental data on both true and 
      fallible disease counts at various covariate levels. We present a method for 
      incorporating such supplemental data into disease rate regression and use it to 
      show that, although observed intercountry differences in European cervical cancer 
      mortality rates are exaggerated by errors in death certification, they are not 
      completely explained by such errors." The data concern Belgium, England and 
      Wales, France, and Italy.
