IS  - 0197-5897 (Linking)
VI  - 12
IP  - 4
DP  - 1991 Winter
TI  - Communicable disease mortality: now you see it, now you don't.
PG  - 464-74
AB  - This presentation proposes that cause-specific mortality analyses are greatly 
      enhanced by first examining the cause-specific pattern of the entire mortality 
      structure instead of restricting initial assessments to a limited number of 
      leading causes of death. Six broad cause groups are defined toward this end. The 
      advantage of defining a single category for communicable diseases, both for the 
      structural and the leading-cause approach is also pointed out. Some examples 
      illustrate the potential usefulness of this approach to the study of the 
      cause-specific mortality structure: a few broad all-inclusive cause-groups 
      provide a first rough--but nevertheless quite informative--overview of the 
      mortality profile, while at the same time offering guidance in regard to groups 
      which should be looked into in greater detail.
FAU - Plaut, R R
AU  - Plaut RR
FAU - Silvi, J J
