TI  - Clinical causes and classification of perinatal mortality in Lagos.
PG  - 443-7
AB  - Perinatal deaths in singleton births at the Lagos University Teaching Hospital 
      during a 5-year period were reviewed. Causes of deaths were classified into eight 
      groups using a modified form of the Aberdeen classification. Perinatal mortality 
      was high (42.5/1000 total births). The stillbirth rate was 32.5/1000 total 
      births. The major causes of perinatal mortality were trauma (30.5%), low birth 
      weight (23.9%), hemorrhage (13.7%), toxemia of pregnancy (10.3%) and mature, 
      cause unknown (10%). Congenital malformation (4.3%) was not a major cause of 
      perinatal deaths in this study.
