TI  - Children from broken homes: visits to the school nurse.
PG  - 189-94
AB  - Children from broken homes, especially females, have an increased tendency to 
      visit the school nurse. Complaints are often ill-defined, possibly psychosomatic. 
      These children may require additional medical and emotional support from the 
      school nurse. The effect the broken home may have upon a student has important 
      implications for the physical and emotional health of today's youth. An awareness 
      of this finding can provide school nursing personnel valuable insight in the 
      assessment of students who visit the school nurse.
